SUMMARY:An affirmative solution to the generalized Busemann-Petty problem w
 ith subspaces dimensions 2 and 3
DESCRIPTION:The generalized Busemann--Petty problem asks whether two origin
 -symmetric convex bodies in $\\mathbb{R}^n$ having larger volume of all $m
 $-dimensional sections necessarily have larger volume. When $m\\geq 4$\, t
 his is known to be false\, but the cases $m=2\, 3$ for $n\\geq 5$ have rem
 ained open since the 1990s. In this work\, we resolve these cases. Togethe
 r with the known results\, the generalized…\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr
 /event/17073/
